Tru64 UNIX Version 5.0, like some other UNIX
flavors (but with its own twists) uses a TCB
database that controls additional security
features, many of which can be set/controlled
on a per-user basis.  It seems several of these
UNIX flavors use a common code base from
Secureware, if I'm not mistaken.  (Other
examples: HP-UX, SCO UNIX)

references:
http://h30097.www3.hp.com/docs/base_doc/DOCUMENTATION/V50_HTML/ARH95ATE/TITLE.HTM
