If you're not running Enhanced Security try:
As root, vipw, delete the contents of the password field for the user.
or
As the user or root, use the passwd command to change the password.
When it tells you the password must be at least 6 characters keep trying.
Eventually it will let you set the null password.

To check if the system is running Enhanced Security, as root:
# rcmgr get SECURITY

If the system is running Enhanced Security, you can find documentation
in the Security manual and the man pages for: usermod, edauth,
prpasswd.

